[NEW] &lt;p&gt;Business end-users and buyers can define and maintain their own outbound follow-up scenarios and use them wherever built-in scenarios are used today:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scenario maintenance — a dedicated setup page where users create, edit, and maintain custom follow-up scenarios. Each scenario carries (GA: December CY2026) — Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management

[UPDATED] &lt;p&gt;Model-driven apps now support configurable display density settings that let users choose how information is spaced throughout the application. Users can select from three density options:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable (default)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cozy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compact&lt;br&gt;
​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each density setting a (GA: November CY2026) — Power Apps

&lt;p&gt;Currently, to bring tasks from another project into a new project, you must manually enter the task details in the task grid or use schedule APIs. You can also use the &lt;strong&gt;Copy project&lt;/strong&gt; feature to create a new project with the same tasks, but this feature has limitations:&lt;br&gt;
​&lt;/p&gt;
